.TH INVF-FUSE 8 "2026-09" "InvariantFS" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
invf-fuse \- mount an InvariantFS volume via FUSE
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B invf-fuse
.RB [ \-f ]
.RB [ \-o
.IR opt [, opt ...]]
.I image mountpoint
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B invf-fuse
is the InvariantFS FUSE daemon. It mounts the volume stored in
.I image
(a regular file or a block device) at
.IR mountpoint .
Without
.B \-f
the daemon detaches into the background after a successful mount; with
.B \-f
it stays in the foreground.
.PP
The daemon adds the mount options
.BR attr_timeout=1 , ac_attr_timeout=1 , entry_timeout=1
and
.B max_read=1048576
by default, and tags the mount source as
.BI invfs[ basename ]
so
.BR mount (8)
output and
/proc/mounts
identify the volume. User-supplied
.B \-o
options come later and win.
.PP
SIGTERM/SIGINT shut the daemon down cleanly: the volume is closed with a
CLEAN superblock. A DIRTY volume with an anomaly-free scan self-heals to
CLEAN+rw at the next mount (see
.BR invf-fsck (8)).
.SH OPTIONS
In addition to the standard
.BR fuse (8)
options, the following InvariantFS-specific options are consumed before the
list reaches libfuse:
.TP
.BI arc_limit= K | M | G
ARC cache budget for decoded units (default 256M, or
.BR INVFS_ARC_BYTES ).
A whole-file decode unit larger than half the budget is refused at sweep
time; the read path never refuses stored data.
.TP
.BI dec_mem_limit= K | M | G
Per-unit decoder working-set limit (default 512M, or
.BR INVFS_DEC_MEM_LIMIT ).
Codecs whose decode needs more are declined at sweep time and the file falls
back to generic storage.
.TP
.BR at_checkpoint [ =seq ]
Mount the read-only view at a live sweep checkpoint (WP21/WP24). Without
.IR seq ,
the live checkpoint is used (K=1 contract).
.TP
.BI attr_t= seconds
Attribute/entry cache TTL (default 1.0;
.B 0
disables kernel caching entirely so every stat hits the daemon).
.TP
.BI raw_watermark= pct
RAW-zone fill percent that makes the daemon kick an early checkpoint-armed
sweep (WP26); 0 disables. See
.BR INVFS_RAW_WATERMARK .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B INVFS_SWEEP_INTERVAL
Seconds between automatic background sweeps. Unset (default) means
.IR no
background sweeping: automatic transcoding of a root filesystem is
deliberately opt-in. A manual pass is triggered by
.BR "kill \-USR1" ,
by
.BR setfattr " \-n user.invfs.sweep \-v 1 /"
inside the mount (root only), or by
.BR invf-sweep (8)
run offline.
.TP
.B INVFS_PROFILE
Codec effort profile:
.BR fast | balanced | dense | archive
(default
.BR balanced ;
an unset variable reproduces existing volumes byte-identically). The profile
is re-exported to codecpack helper processes.
.TP
.B INVFS_CODECPACKS
Colon-separated extra directories scanned for
.B *.codecpack
packs before
.BR /usr/lib/invfs/codecpacks .
.TP
.B INVFS_TOOLS
Directory searched first for external codec tools, before
.B /usr/lib/invfs/tools
and PATH.
.TP
.B INVFS_AUTO_RECOVER
Set to 0 to disable the DIRTY-volume auto-recovery at mount.
.TP
.B INVFS_ARC_BYTES , INVFS_DEC_MEM_LIMIT
Fallbacks for the
.BR \-o " arc_limit" / dec_mem_limit
mount options.
.SH CONTROL INTERFACE
The mount root carries a control namespace:
.PP
.nf
getfattr --only-values -n user.invfs /        # RAM summary
getfattr --only-values -n user.invfs.stats /  # hot counters + zone usage
setfattr -n user.invfs.sweep -v 1 /           # trigger a manual sweep (root)
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; non-zero if the volume cannot be opened or the mount fails.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR invf-mkfs (8),
.BR invf-sweep (8),
.BR invf-fsck (8),
.BR invarifs (7),
.BR fuse (8)
